 "formula": "Main level L=99, support level S=49+floor(ML/5) (0 / no contribution without a support job), ML=Master Level 0..50. Curves are run-length tables in scales: cumulative(curve,column,N) = sum of the per-level gains for levels 1..N (row at level 1 is the starting value). ATTRIBUTES (STR..CHR): graded curve scales.attributes.graded is in twentieths of a point and stops growing after level 75. half(grade,N)=floor(cumulative(graded,grade,min(N,75))/10) = value in half points. attr = floor( ( half(raceGrade,L) + half(mainJobGrade,L) + floor(half(subJobGrade,S)/2) ) / 2 ) + over75(L) + ML, where over75(99)=18 (scales.attributes.ungraded: +1 per level 76-99 except 76,80,85,89,94,98; main level only). I.e. race + main job at full value, support job at half of its own-level value, pooled in half points and floored once (current retail, round_once=true). HP = cumulative(hp.racial, race, L) + cumulative(hp.graded, mainJob.HP grade, L) + floor(cumulative(hp.graded, subJob.HP grade, S)/2) + 7*ML. Race HP uses its own per-race curve (flat after 75), NOT the race letter grade; the 61+ / 76+ slow-down terms are already inside the curves. MP: if main job has an MP grade: MP = cumulative(mp.racial, race, L) + cumulative(mp.graded, mainJob.MP, L) + floor(cumulative(mp.graded, subJob.MP, S)/2) (sub term 0 if sub has no MP grade) + 2*ML. If main job has no MP grade but support job has: MP = floor(cumulative(mp.racial, race, S)/2) + floor(cumulative(mp.graded, subJob.MP, S)/2) (race part taken at the SUPPORT level and halved; no Master Level MP). If neither has an MP grade: MP = 0. Job-trait Max HP Boost / Max MP Boost (WAR, MNK, PLD, NIN, RUN / SMN, SCH, GEO, BLU spells) are NOT included; they are added on top in the HP/MP shown in game. Master Level: +1 to each of the 7 attributes, +7 max HP, +2 max MP (main jobs with native MP only) per level, cap 50; support job level cap 49+floor(ML/5).",
