 "notes": [
  "Validation: reference_js reproduces all 110 race x job level-99 no-support-job rows and all 2310 race x main99 x sub49 rows of the capture spreadsheet (HP/MP after adding the Max HP/MP Boost trait amounts: HP tiers 30/60/120/180/240/280 then Max HP Boost II 430/580/730; MP tiers 10/20/40/60/80/100; highest tier of main-at-99 or sub-at-49 applies). Trait tier levels per the sheet: WAR 30/50/70/90, MNK 15/25/35/45/55/65 + II at 75/85/95, PLD 45/85, NIN and RUN 20/40/60/80/99; Max MP Boost SMN 10/30/50/70/76/96, GEO 30/60/90, SCH 30/88. BLU gets them only from set spells.",
  "The capture sheet has no data for support levels 50-59 or for Master Levels; LandSandBoat does not implement Master Levels. ML samples are computed (curves at sub level 50-59 + BG Wiki per-ML bonuses) and are unverified against retail.",
  "Master Level text, BG Wiki Master_Levels: \"As of the November 10th, 2022 Version Update, the cap on Master Levels is 50 per job. Every Master Level earned, the player receives the following for that job: +1 STR, DEX, VIT, AGI, INT, MND, and CHR per level; +1 to the cap of Combat Skills and Magic Skills per level (Only skills that are learned naturally for the job that gained a Master level will be increased...); +7 Maximum HP per level; +2 Maximum MP per level\". Also: \"For every five master levels your earn, your support job level cap will be increased by 1.\" BG Wiki Support_Job: \"Support Job = 49 + floor(Master Level/5)\". Pets also gain stats (see page). \"Every master level you gain effectively raises your character level by 1\" (affects /check, level correction).",
  "wiki.ffo.jp マスターレベル: 「マスターレベルが1上昇するごとに、プレイヤー及びペットの全基礎パラメータと戦闘／魔法スキル上限がそれぞれ+1上昇し、HPとMP(メインで所持しているジョブのみ)も上昇する。」「マスターレベルの上限は50、サポートジョブは59となっている。」 -> MP bonus only for main jobs that natively have MP (implemented that way). The JP page gives no HP/MP amounts; +7/+2 are from BG Wiki only.",
  "Disagreement: BG Wiki Support_Job lists \"Base MP by race (Level 75+)\" for MP-less main jobs as Tarutaru 116 / Hume 59 / Mithra 59 / Elvaan 40 / Galka 11. Those equal the pre-2014 formula at sub level 37 and do NOT match current captures: e.g. captured Hume WAR99/WHM49 MP = 229 = floor(254/2) racial + floor(204/2) WHM. The capture-backed LandSandBoat rule is used here (race part at level 49: Hume/Mithra 127, Elvaan 102, Tarutaru 152, Galka 76).",
  "Race HP/MP letter grades in \"races\" are informational only (from grades.yaml; identical on wiki.ffo.jp ステータス). Since the April 2014 update racial HP/MP follow the per-race curves in scales.hp.racial / scales.mp.racial; race letters ARE used for the 7 attributes. Job grade letters match wiki.ffo.jp ステータス for all 22 jobs.",
  "The older LandSandBoat/DSP HPScale/MPScale arrays (base, <30, <60, <75 scale columns) still exist in grades.cpp but are no longer used for player HP/MP; the level-by-level curves in data/stats.yaml replaced them.",
  "Point 4 (white vs green): no wiki statement found. Evidence from LandSandBoat (mirrors the retail status packet): merit attribute points are added into the base attribute array (bp_base = white number) and HP/MP merits into max HP/MP; equipment/food/buff modifiers go to bp_adj (green +N). The capture sheet states \"Test characters have 0 merits\", consistent with merits being inside the base number. Job Point gifts grant no STR..CHR/HP/MP base values (they are attack/accuracy/skill etc. modifiers). Where Master Level attribute points are displayed (white vs green) was not confirmed by any source read; they are permanent per-job values and are treated as base here.",
  "BLU: attribute/HP/MP bonuses from set blue magic are not part of this calculation.",
  "BG Wiki race pages (Category:Hume etc.) have mostly empty/outdated stat tables and were not usable for level 99 values; BG Wiki pages \"Attributes\", \"Character_Stats\", \"Magic_Points\" do not exist."
 ]
}